(4819668, 693277, 15291, '<td valign="top">Hi Stan,<br/>       Looks as if you got caught out in no-mans land here. I think the combination of the high iso, all the PPing &amp; the crop left you with lots of nosie. It also seems to be a bit out of focus. The background greens are nice but the white is a bit of a distraction. Not sure why so high on the iso, I am assuming it was windy., and overall I think there was way to much PPing  for this subject. What I do like is the fact you where able to get a real nice range of colors in the greens.</td>', 'Hi Stan,       Looks as if you got caught out in no-mans land here. I think the combination of the high iso, all the PPing & the crop left you with lots of nosie. It also seems to be a bit out of focus. The background greens are nice but the white is a bit of a distraction. Not sure why so high on the iso, I am assuming it was windy., and overall I think there was way to much PPing  for this subject. What I do like is the fact you where able to get a real nice range of colors in the greens.', '2008-07-11 17:59:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(4819715, 693300, 15291, '<td valign="top">Hi Kat,<br/>      First I''d like to say this is a great take on the challenge &amp; the title fits really well. I like the way u set your elements in relation to your subject, it is composted &amp; framed very nicely. I see you used &amp; iso of 800 this is nicely done there is very little nosie if any at all that I can see, nice job there. I also like the tonality of the overall image. The one thing I do see here &amp; I am not sure there is much you could have done about it was the position of the sun/clouds your foreground is nicely lit and it seems to fade as we go back into the image. There doesn''t seem to be enough light on the trees/bush which caused a loss of detail in them, this could have rescued in pping maybe. Overall thou I like the tonality &amp; balance of the image. This is a really nice image, great job.<br/></td>', 'Hi Kat,      First I''d like to say this is a great take on the challenge & the title fits really well. I like the way u set your elements in relation to your subject, it is composted & framed very nicely. I see you used & iso of 800 this is nicely done there is very little nosie if any at all that I can see, nice job there. I also like the tonality of the overall image. The one thing I do see here & I am not sure there is much you could have done about it was the position of the sun/clouds your foreground is nicely lit and it seems to fade as we go back into the image. There doesn''t seem to be enough light on the trees/bush which caused a loss of detail in them, this could have rescued in pping maybe. Overall thou I like the tonality & balance of the image. This is a really nice image, great job.', '2008-07-11 18:35:27.000000', NULL, 0),
